claims.text:
🟡 **Medium**

**Hardcoded call index makes summary assertion unreliable**

This index (`[5]`) will silently break if any earlier `generateObject` call is added or removed. Scanning for the call by a distinguishing property (e.g., the system prompt containing `"ground truth"`) is more robust and was already recommended by a prior reviewer.

Suggested replacement:
```ts
const summaryCall = (mockGenerateObject as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mock.calls
  .find((c) => (c[0].system as string)?.includes("ground truth"))?.[0];
expect(summaryCall).toBeDefined();
const summaryPrompt = summaryCall.messages[0].content as string;
expect(summaryPrompt).toContain("Bug");
```

*Suggested fix:*

```suggestion
    const summaryCall = (mockGenerateObject as ReturnType<typeof vi.fn>).mock.calls
      .find((c) => (c[0].system as string)?.includes("ground truth"))?.[0];
    expect(summaryCall).toBeDefined();
    const summaryPrompt = summaryCall!.messages[0].content as string;
    expect(summaryPrompt).toContain("Bug");
```
